# Build outputs from `zig build`. Both are directories rather than single files
# because a normal user build creates them, and a normal user build must not
# dirty the tree or leak into a package published from it.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own output
# tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore so that a build
# run from the repository root cannot be committed by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/

# Nix and devenv working directories. `devenv shell` creates `.devenv/` and
# `nix develop` through .envrc creates `.direnv/`; both are state, not source,
# and both belong outside a commit and outside a flake source. `package.nix`
# filters them by name as well, so the Nix output is clean whether or not this
# file is consulted.
.devenv/
.direnv/

# A Nix build leaves a `result` symlink at the flake root pointing into the
# store. It names a store path that changes on every rebuild, so committing it
# would be recording a build receipt in the source tree.
/result